{
  "slug": "artist:ice-t",
  "name": "Ice-T",
  "editorial_article": "Born Tracy Lauren Marrow, the Newark-raised artist moved to Los Angeles where he became a foundational architect of West Coast gangsta rap. After debuting with the 1983 electro track 'Cold Wind Madness' on Saturn Records, he gained mainstream attention with 'Reckless,' a 1984 single produced by Chris 'The Glove' Taylor for the breakdance film Breakin'. His debut studio album, 1987's Rhyme Pays, featured production by Afrika Islam and secured a deal with Sire Records. In 1990, he introduced his heavy metal band Body Count on the O.G. Original Gangster album track of the same name. His 1993 album Home Invasion, distributed via Priority Records, contained the original version of '99 Problems.' Beyond his music, he has maintained a long-term role as Detective Odafin Tutuola on Law & Order: Special Victims Unit.",
